# Firmum Model Selection — Quick Examples

**Full tier table and queue:** See `model-gate-b2c-parity.mdc` and `.cursor/b2c-parity-queue.md`.

**Never use Grok** unless the user names Grok in that message. **Never use Codex.**

## Composer-safe (G0) — cheapest, use by default for these

- Add route + lazy import in `App.tsx`
- Mirror backend data to frontend constants (e.g. `tier_catalog.py` → `b2cTiers.ts`)
- Marketing copy, FAQ, comparison rows
- Extend `mock_b2c.py` / E2E mock payloads
- `env.example` placeholders
- Fix unused imports, implicit `any`, post-Sonnet build breaks
- Shell scaffolds, build commands, deploy commands

## GPT 5.6 Sol (G0.5) — pattern clones and bulk work

- Clone portal page → client page (e.g. `PortalGoals.tsx` → `ClientGoals.tsx`)
- Bulk mock payload generation (30+ transactions, 8 advisors)
- Chart components from existing data structures
- Post-Sonnet TypeScript cleanup across multiple files
- Docs from gold-standard templates

## Sonnet-required (G1) — do NOT use Composer or GPT 5.6

- Plaid Link token exchange, transaction sync, token storage
- Stripe webhooks, subscription state, advisor connect billing
- Entitlements / tier gating changes
- Auth flows (forgot password, session management, 2FA)
- New layout shells with auth-aware navigation
- Alembic migrations (design + implement; Opus review if complex)
- Auth scope / 404-not-403 enforcement
- Unified client shell (DIY + advisor-linked modes)

## Opus (G2) — review/unblock only, never default implementer

- IDOR / cross-tenant access checks
- Webhook signature validation review
- Token encryption audit
- AI guardrails review (no investment advice)
- Complex migration review
